// Pull request: #6474 new: AOMEI Backupper supply chain compromise rules
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/6474
// Pull request author: veeramani-sl-12207
// Change: new rule
// Title: Suspicious AOMEI ABNotify Child Process From Html Directory
// Sigma ID: 3768e7d0-ba38-48fa-a630-d25bb50438de
// Status: experimental | Level: high
// Author: Veeramani
// Date: 2026-06-11 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1036.005
// Description: Detects ABNotify.exe, running from the standard AOMEI Backupper installation path, spawning any
//   executable located in the html\ rendering hierarchy. This directory is intended for rendering
//   assets, not executables; a child process launched from here indicates a hijacked upgrade
//   workflow triggered through the AOMEI notification agent with no user interaction.
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://www.manageengine.com/threat-analysis-lab/aomei-backupper-supply-chain-compromise.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/75d1b797f7a71e9406d0482f2ac78f3b999da317/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_aomei_abnotify_susp_child_from_html_dir.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (InitiatingProcessFolderPath contains "\\AOMEI\\AOMEI Backupper\\" and InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\ABNotify.exe") and ((FolderPath contains "\\AOMEI\\AOMEI Backupper\\" and FolderPath contains "\\html\\") and FolderPath endswith ".exe")
